{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D7]All I know is [D7]something like a bird
[D7]within her sang,[D7][C][D7][C][D7]
[D7]All I know she sang [D7]a little while
[D7]and then flew off,[D7][C][D7][C][D7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Tell [F]me [F]all [C]that you know,
[C]I'll [G]show you      [G]snow and rain.[D7][D7][D7][D7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
If you hear that same sweet song again,
will you know why?
Anyone who sings a tune so sweet
is passin' by,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Laugh in the sunshine, sing,
cry in the dark, fly through the night.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Bm]Don't          [Bm][A]cry   [A]now,
[G]don't [D]you [A]cry, [G]don't [D]you [A]cry anymore,[G]
[G]la-da-da-da.[D][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[Bm]Sleep       [Bm]in the [A]stars,
[G]don't [D]you [A]cry, [G]dry [D]your [A]eyes on the wind,[G]
[G]la-da-da-da-da.[D][D7][D]
{end_of_verse}

